                "role": "assistant",
                "content": "To create a $21 \\times 21$ board where there are exactly $11$ rows with a majority of blue cells and exactly $11$ columns with a majority of red cells, and to ensure that the largest monochromatic square has a side length of $10$, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Divide the Board**: We can divide the board into four quadrants, each of size $10 \\times 10$, with a central $1 \\times 1$ cell separating them.\n2. **Coloring Strategy**:\n   - Color the top-left quadrant and bottom-right quadrant entirely blue.\n   - Color the top-right quadrant and bottom-left quadrant entirely red.\n   - The central cell can be either color, but for simplicity, let's make it blue.\n\nHere's how this would look:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{array}{ccccccccccccccccccccc}\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b \\\\\nr & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b \\\\\nr & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b \\\\\nr & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b \\\\\nr & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b \\\\\nr & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b \\\\\nr & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b \\\\\nr & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b \\\\\nr & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b \\\\\nr & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b \\\\\nr & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b \\\\\n\\end{array}}\n\\]\n\nIn this configuration:\n- Each of the $10 \\times 10$ blue squares (top-left and bottom-right) ensures that $10$ rows and $10$ columns have a majority of blue cells.\n- Each of the $10 \\times 10$ red squares (top-right and bottom-left) ensures that $10$ rows and $10$ columns have a majority of red cells.\n- The central cell being blue adds one more row and column with a majority of blue cells, making a total of $11$ rows and $11$ columns with the required majorities.\n\nThe largest monochromatic square has a side length of $10$, as desired."
